WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.420
- Technology and the
way we live doesn't care

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.540
about my opinion or my feelings

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.460
and it doesn't care about yours either.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.487
And so you can walk
around earth and judge,

00:00:10.487 --> 00:00:13.537
"Oh, it's so sad that all
these kids can't communicate,

00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:15.120
"'cause they're on the phone anymore."

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.080
And you can talk about a day
and age when it was simpler,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.231
and nicer, and all this,
nobody gives a fuck.

00:00:21.231 --> 00:00:22.491
(audience laughing)

00:00:22.491 --> 00:00:23.400
(audience applauding)

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.200
And if you don't adjust to
the reality of the situation,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.060
you will be completely left behind.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:32.343
Too many people are executing, or hoping,

00:00:32.343 --> 00:00:35.220
or trying to figure out
how to live in a world

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.080
that used to be or the
way they wish it was,

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.890
versus attacking the reality of the world.

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.730
And here is the reality
of the world my friends.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.800
The cellphones that you're
all holding right now,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.740
or in your pocket, are the
remote controls of our society.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.000
They are the single most
important thing in the world.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.330
There's nothing close.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.270
Whatever you want to happen in life,

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.470
you first need somebody's attention,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.400
and then you need to tell them about it.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.250
It was called the newspaper,
the television, and the radio.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.858
Now it's called a blog,
a vlog, or a podcast.

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:11.110
It's the same thing, nothing's
changed except one thing.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:14.090
Your attention is moving to a new place,

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.660
and leaving an old place.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.426
I'm making this very simple,

00:01:17.426 --> 00:01:21.280
very black and white, very fucking basic.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.800
If you do not spend next year

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.560
completely obsessing over
how you become successful

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.490
on Facebook and Instagram,

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:32.480
you will be disproportionally
less likely to win.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.920
The ad product on those two platforms

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.323
are disproportionally underpriced,

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:41.350
and that that is where
you should be trading.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.393
You are grossly underestimating
what's happening right now.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.480
98% of people are grossly underestimating

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.770
how good it is, right?

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.300
You will look back at this talk,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.560
all my content during this era,

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:59.382
why am I producing so much
content during this era?

00:01:59.382 --> 00:02:03.630
Why am I flying around the
entire world over and over,

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.330
speaking to this subject?

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.250
It's because I know what
I'm talking about right now,

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.423
is gonna go away.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.670
And I think we can all agree,

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.159
I'm not hedging up here right now.

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:14.860
(audience chuckling)

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.343
I'm desperately trying to force this

00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:19.830
down your fucking mouth, right?

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.920
You heard it, and I believe that 95%

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.860
of you will not do anything about it.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.653
You'll do enough to make it
feel like you did something,

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.190
and you will regret not going all in.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:33.790
How many people here play poker?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.183
Good, I don't, but if you do,

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.961
when you have the best hand,
it's a good idea to go all in.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:45.270
I'm a great entrepreneur
but I think I'm even better

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.690
at consumer behavior and psychology.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.540
It's who I am, it's why
a lot of you follow me,

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.631
because when you cut me down

00:02:50.631 --> 00:02:52.623
you see that I'm pushing positivity,

00:02:52.623 --> 00:02:54.469
and a whole lot of other
things that matter,

00:02:54.469 --> 00:02:56.450
and trying to get people
to do it the right way.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:59.210
Be patient, do the
right thing, dadadadada.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.604
The thing that people have
not wrapped their head around,

00:03:01.604 --> 00:03:05.670
is that this takes a lot
of work, like a lot a lot.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:09.892
If you want to make $100,000
a year and like doing it,

00:03:09.892 --> 00:03:13.681
and it's on your terms,
and it's your life,

00:03:13.681 --> 00:03:18.430
it takes a lot of work, and
it takes a lot of smart work.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.810
You've never met anybody in your life

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.920
who hasn't worked their
face off for a long time

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.000
that's built something significant.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.900
It may seem that it happened
fast 'cause they're 27,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.614
but maybe they've been
hustling since they were 13

00:03:29.614 --> 00:03:32.692
in a different way that gave
them 14 years of experience

00:03:32.692 --> 00:03:34.500
to be a winner in that game.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.600
Everybody's so worried about tomorrow

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.433
that it doesn't allow them

00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:40.250
to see what's actually happening here.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.904
And that why I always
recommend people spending time

00:03:41.904 --> 00:03:44.930
with older people, retirement home.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.210
I'm a big fan because you get

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:49.130
to see regret and resentment up close,

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.380
and it starts to help you frame up a life.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.120
In life we're all born

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.500
with either an advantage or disadvantage.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.740
We either started with too much,

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.450
or we started with too little,

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.100
and then basically, you know,

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:04.850
your internal fortitude decides
if that was good or bad.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.520
You know, listen man, to
be very honest with you,

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.450
I'll give you answer.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:11.763
You have no choice, that's how.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.380
What's the alternative?

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.010
When you have a setback,
what are you gonna sit there

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.000
and say it was your granddad and your dad?

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.470
I mean, you know that's not true.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.970
It's why you have so many wins, right?

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.380
So just practice.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.190
I just kept practicing
blaming myself for everything.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.550
Now I just default into it.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.665
I think you just have now choice, brother.

00:04:29.665 --> 00:04:31.490
Listen, I'll leave you guys with this.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:35.300
Doing anything that doesn't ring true

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.360
down your entire
operating system and soul,

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.900
because you think you need to do it

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.200
based on somebody's
advice that you admire,

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.850
or because you have
short-term pain in your life,

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.464
is never going to work.

00:04:46.464 --> 00:04:49.620
It has never worked, it doesn't work,

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.070
and it's just better to wrap your head

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:55.671
around enjoying the short-term
pain, and I mean that.

00:04:55.671 --> 00:04:59.440
Listen, the Rocky movies that
are good is when it's shitty,

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.591
not when he's in the fancy mansion.

00:05:01.591 --> 00:05:04.210
If you're sitting with
some adversity right now,

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:06.570
it's yours, right?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:10.310
No matter what your
adversity is, we all have it.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.813
And so please, please wrap your head

00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:14.700
around what we're actually doing here.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.470
And more importantly,
if you were smart enough

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.537
to be here today, and I mean this.

00:05:19.537 --> 00:05:21.600
The fact that you came here today

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.560
puts you so far ahead of everybody else,

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:28.380
and I hate knowing for a fact

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:31.240
that so many of you are going
to give up your advantage,

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.810
because you like hearing me say it,

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.800
and you like the way it feels,

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.177
but then you leave and you
don't do anything about it.

00:05:38.177 --> 00:05:40.610
So please Brisbane, do me a favor,

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.260
go do something about this talk today.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:47.070
I implore you, it will change
the course of your career.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:47.903
Thank you.

00:05:47.903 --> 00:05:48.899
(audience applauding)

00:05:48.899 --> 00:05:51.316
(soft music)

